  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $0\\in {0,1}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $1\\in {0,1}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $2\\in {2,3,5,7}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $3\\in {2,3,5,7}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $4\\in {4,8}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $5\\in {2,3,5,7}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $6$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $7\\in {2,3,5,7}$\n\n- $8\\in {4,8}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $9$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $10$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe elements $6,9,$ and $10$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${6,9,10}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
